  "articleBody": "When you're looking to make your home safer with slip-resistant flooring, it's easy to stumble into a few common pitfalls. Here are some mistakes to avoid: \n1. **Ignoring the room's function:** Don't just pick a floor because it looks good. A bathroom floor needs different slip resistance than a basement floor. Always match the flooring to the specific needs and moisture levels of the room. \n2. **Prioritizing aesthetics over safety:** While you want your home to look great, the primary goal of slip-resistant flooring is safety. Make sure the aesthetic choices don't compromise its effectiveness. \n3. **Assuming all textured floors are slip-resistant:** Some textures can actually trap water and become slick. Look for specific slip-resistance ratings or talk to an expert. \n4. **Forgetting about cleaning and maintenance:** Some slip-resistant floors can be harder to clean due to their texture. Make sure you understand the maintenance requirements before committing. \n5. **DIY installation without experience:** Proper installation is crucial for the flooring to perform as intended. If you're not experienced, leave it to the professionals. \n6. **Not consulting an expert:** An experienced general contractor like HH Remodeling LLC can help you navigate the options, avoid these mistakes, and ensure you get the best and safest solution for your home in areas like Denver, Centennial, or Aurora.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
